lity, noted starting 2023, is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex processes and agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high visibility standards and ethical practices. [Data: Sources (3912, 1782), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 10), (2024, 12, 09))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between various SAP departments, established in 2023, ensures that technological strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (3913, 3914), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 10), (2024, 01, 01))]\n\n## Generative AI Hub\n\nThe Generative AI Hub at SAP includes prompt experimentation, prompt management, and administrative tools. Prompt experimentation includes creating and running natural language prompts with a choice of large language models and parameters. Prompt management includes saving prompts with collections, metadata in the form of tags and notes, versioning, and deletion. For more information, see Generative AI Hub in SAP AI Core Overview. [Data: Sources (3704, 3705), Date_Range ((2023, 12, 20), (2024, 01, 01))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services\n\nCloud Identity Services at SAP have been upgraded, providing enhanced security and compliance features. Their focus on identity management and access control, noted starting 2024, is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex identities and access control. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high security standards and ethical practices. [Data: Sources (2871, 2872), Date_Range ((2024, 05, 22), (2024, 12, 21))]", "# SAP Technology and Finance Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of key SAP departments focusing on technology and finance, highlighting their interactions and impact on the organizational framework. The information is relevant to the company's operations as of 2025.\n\n## Technology Department Operational Scope\n\nThe Technology Department at SAP plays a pivotal role in developing and maintaining the company's technological infrastructure. Their proactive approach, highlighted in 2024 and 2025, helps safeguard SAP against potential technological pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective technology management not only prevents operational anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (3701, 3702, 3703), Date_Range ((2023, 12, 20), (2025, 07, 29))]\n\n## Finance Department Operational Scope\n\nThe Finance Department at SAP ensures that all financial operations adhere to the legal standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on financial management and compliance, noted in 2024, is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex financial transactions and corporate agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high financial standards and ethical practices. [Data: Sources (1741, 1742, 1743), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 02), (2025, 07, 29))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between the Technology and Finance Departments, established in 2024, ensures that technological strategies are financially sound and that financial measures consider technological risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating technology management with financial compliance strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (3701, 3702, 3703), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2025, 07, 29))]", "# SAP Technology Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key departments focusing on technology, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to uphold technological standards and manage software updates effectively. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2024.\n\n## SAP Build Process Automation Operational Scope\n\nThe SAP Build Process Automation Department at SAP plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating software risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2024, helps safeguard SAP against potential software pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents software anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (1, 2), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 04, 08))]\n\n## Integration Advisor and Trading Partner Management\n\nThe Integration Advisor and Trading Partner Management Departments ensure that all SAP's operations adhere to the technological standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on software updates and trading partner management, noted starting 2024, is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex software updates and trading partner agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high technological standards and ethical practices. [Data: Sources (3, 4), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 04, 08))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between the SAP Build Process Automation, Integration Advisor, and Trading Partner Management Departments, established in 2024, ensures that software updates are legally sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (5, 6), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 04, 08))]\n\n## SAP Conversational AI Community Edition\n\nThe SAP Conversational AI community edition will no longer be available after December 31, 2023. Licensed users can migrate productive bots to the enterprise edition of the platform to ensure uninterrupted conversation experience for their users. This change is crucial for maintaining the company's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex software updates and trading partner agreements. [Data: Source (7), Date_Range ((2023, 12, 31), (2024, 01, 01))]\n\n## Cloud Integration Software Updates\n\nThe Cloud Integration Department at SAP plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating software risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2025, helps safeguard SAP against potential software pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents software anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (8, 9), Date_Range ((2025, 09, 07), (2025, 09, 07))]\n\n## Java Server Software Updates\n\nThe Java Server Department at SAP plays a crucial role in ensuring that all SAP's operations adhere to the technological standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on software updates, noted starting 2025, is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex software updates and trading partner agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high technological standards and ethical practices. [Data: Sources (10, 11), Date_Range ((2025, 09, 04), (2025, 09, 04))]", "# SAP Technology and Finance Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key departments focusing on technology and finance, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to uphold regulatory standards and manage financial risks effectively. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2025.\n\n## SAP Technology Operational Scope\n\nThe SAP Technology Department plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating financial risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2025, helps safeguard SAP against potential financial pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents financial anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (510, 511), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 05, 28))]\n\n## SAP Finance and Compliance\n\nThe SAP Finance Department ensures that all SAP's operations adhere to the legal standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on corporate governance and contract management, noted starting Q2 2024, is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex contracts and corporate agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high legal standards and ethical practices. [Data: Source (378), Date_Range ((2024, 04, 01), (2025, 03, 16))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between the SAP Technology and Finance Departments, established in Q2 2024, ensures that risk mitigation strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (1684, 1686), Date_Range ((2024, 04, 01), (2025, 03, 16))]", "# SAP BTP Community Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of the SAP BTP community, highlighting key entities, their relationships, and significant program-specific or eligibility-related insights. The information is relevant to the community's operations as of 2024.\n\n## SAP BTP Services and Capabilities\n\nSAP BTP offers a range of services and capabilities, including Application Logging Service, Kyma Runtime, and SAP Build Process Automation. These services enable customers to build, deploy, and manage applications on the platform. Effective use of these services is critical for achieving business outcomes and driving innovation. [Data: Sources (251, 3149, 3150), Date_Range ((2024, 04, 01), (2024, 04, 10))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between various departments and services, such as Risk Management and Legal Compliance, is essential for ensuring that risk mitigation strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at SAP BTP. [Data: Sources (9, 3121, 3122), Date_Range ((2020, 01, 01), (2024, 04, 10))]\n\n## New Commercial Model and Services\n\nThe introduction of new commercial models, such as SAP BTP Enterprise Agreement (SAP BTPEA), and services, such as Custom Domain Service and Object Store, has enhanced the capabilities of SAP BTP. These changes have improved flexibility and reduced costs for customers, making SAP BTP a more attractive option for businesses. [Data: Sources (3181, 3182, 3186), Date_Range ((2024, 04, 01), (2024, 04, 10))]", "# SAP Technology Updates Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key technology updates, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to enhance operational efficiency and user experience. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations around 2024.\n\n## Kyma Runtime Updates\n\nKyma Runtime has undergone several updates in 2024, including the deprecation of APIRule v1beta1 and the introduction of new features such as the default CIDR range for Nodes changed to 10.250.0.0/16. These updates aim to improve the overall performance and user experience of Kyma Runtime. [Data: Sources (1695, 2030), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]\n\n## SAP Document AI Updates\n\nSAP Document AI has seen significant updates in 2024, including the introduction of new features such as support for payment advice documents in XLS and XLSX file types, improved underlying infrastructure for LLM-usage, and the ability to select schema versions when adding documents or creating templates. These updates aim to enhance the overall performance and user experience of SAP Document AI. [Data: Sources (1699, 2027, 2029), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]\n\n## SAP Build Process Automation Updates\n\nSAP Build Process Automation has undergone several updates in 2024, including the introduction of new functions such as ISLOWERCASE and ISUPPERCASE, and the ability to use two new functions, MINVALUE and MAXVALUE, in decisions. These updates aim to enhance the overall performance and user experience of SAP Build Process Automation. [Data: Sources (1873, 2026), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]", "# SAP Document AI and Kyma Runtime Overview as of 2023-10-09\n\nThis report delves into SAP Document AI and Kyma Runtime, highlighting key features, updates, and improvements in these technologies. The information is relevant to the development and maintenance of these systems as of 2023-10-09.\n\n## SAP Document AI Updates and Improvements\n\nSAP Document AI has undergone several updates and improvements as of 2023-10-09. These include the release of the Telemetry module 1.1.0 in the fast channel, the deprecation of the LogParser API, and the introduction of new features such as the Autosave feature for editing extraction results and the configuration API. These updates aim to enhance the performance and usability of SAP Document AI, supporting business operations and development processes. [Data: Sources (137, 4082, 4083, 4084, 4085), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 09), (2023, 10, 09))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime Updates and Improvements\n\nKyma Runtime has also undergone several updates and improvements as of 2023-10-09. These include the release of the Telemetry module 1.1.0 in the regular channel, the update to version 1.17.3 of the Istio module, and the introduction of new features such as the support for mTLS in the HTTP output of LogPipeline. These updates aim to enhance the performance and usability of Kyma Runtime, supporting business operations and development processes. [Data: Sources (137, 3999, 761, 778), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 09), (2023, 10, 09))]\n\n## Interoperability between SAP Document AI and Kyma Runtime\n\nThe updates and improvements in SAP Document AI and Kyma Runtime have enhanced interoperability between the two systems. This interoperability supports business operations and development processes, allowing for seamless integration and data exchange between the two systems. [Data: Sources (137, 4082, 3999, 761), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 09), (2023, 10, 09))]", "# SAP Technology Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's key technologies, highlighting their core attributes, connections, and noteworthy claims. The information is relevant to SAP's operations as of 2024.\n\n## SAP Document AI Operational Scope\n\nSAP Document AI plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating financial risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2024, helps safeguard SAP against potential financial pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents financial anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (2959, 3551, 3552), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 05, 15))]\n\n## SAP Document AI Enhancements\n\nSAP Document AI has undergone significant enhancements, including improved extraction results for currency, country, and date fields. The service now supports the extraction of quantities with multipliers and supports the following countries/regions for invoice documents: Hungary, Romania, Türkiye, and more. [Data: Sources (3822, 3823, 3824), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 27), (2024, 01, 08))]\n\n## SAP BTP Cockpit Enhancements\n\nSAP BTP Cockpit has introduced several enhancements, including the availability of a new global URL, sorting options in the Account Explorer page, and the introduction of the Horizon theme. The cockpit also supports a dark version called Evening Horizon and black-and-white high-contrast versions for accessibility. [Data: Sources (4032, 4037, 4038), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 19), (2024, 01, 01))]", "# SAP Technology and Finance Overview as of August 2024\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key departments focusing on technology and finance, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to uphold regulatory standards and manage financial risks effectively. The information is relevant to the company's operations around mid-2024.\n\n## Peppol Exchange Enhancements\n\nThe Peppol Exchange at SAP has undergone significant enhancements, including the update of schematron files for various standards such as A-NZ Peppol BIS Billing, XRechnung, and SI-UBL 2.0. These updates will be active in the production environment as of August 24, 2024. Additionally, the options to create participants with FI:OVT and FI:VAT Party ID have been removed from the Master Data Management app, and users must delete existing participants and create them again with the new FI:OVT2 party ID type. [Data: Sources (743, 223), Date_Range ((2024, 08, 23), (2024, 08, 24))]\n\n## SAP Digital Payments Add-On Enhancements\n\nThe SAP Digital Payments Add-On has introduced new features, including the ability to use payment cards or bank accounts that have been registered previously outside the SAP digital payments add-on and the use of payment type icon URLs in payment pages. These enhancements aim to improve the payment process and provide users with more flexibility. [Data: Sources (743, 223), Date_Range ((2024, 08, 23), (2024, 08, 24))]\n\n## SAP Document AI Enhancements\n\nSAP Document AI has undergone several enhancements, including the improvement of machine learning models for invoice, purchase order, and payment advice, and the addition of new features such as the ability to accurately identify date formats in template-based extraction and the enhancement of the Document feature in the basic UI. These updates aim to improve the accuracy and efficiency of document processing. [Data: Sources (743, 223), Date_Range ((2024, 08, 23), (2024, 09, 09))]", "# SAP BTP Community Overview as of December 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of the SAP BTP community, highlighting key entities, their relationships, and significant updates. The information is relevant to the community's operations around December 2024.\n\n## SAP BTP Component Updates\n\nThe SAP BTP community has seen significant updates to its components, including the SAP BTP Command Line Interface, SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime, and SAP Document AI. These updates have improved the user experience, added new features, and enhanced the overall functionality of the components. The updates are crucial for maintaining the community's operational stability and growth. [Data: Sources (260, 262, 483), Date_Range ((2024, 11, 26), (2024, 12, 12))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Innovation\n\nCollaboration between the SAP BTP components has been instrumental in driving innovation within the community. The components have been working together to provide seamless integration, improved user experience, and enhanced functionality. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in aligning the community's strategies with technological advancements. [Data: Sources (260, 262, 483), Date_Range ((2024, 11, 26), (2024, 12, 12))]\n\n## Deprecation of btp CLI Client Versions\n\nThe SAP BTP community has announced the deprecation of btp CLI client versions 2.54 through 2.61. These versions will no longer work after June 30, 2025. The community is advised to update to the latest btp CLI client version to avoid any disruptions. [Data: Sources (483), Date_Range ((2024, 11, 28), (2025, 06, 30))]", "# SAP Cloud Identity Services and Technology Overview as of April 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's Cloud Identity Services and related technologies, highlighting key components, their interactions, and significant updates as of April 2025. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations and strategic planning.\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Updates\n\nCloud Identity Services at SAP have undergone significant updates as of April 2025. These updates include support for Token Exchange (RFC 8693) and JWT Bearer grant types, taking into account risk-based authentication (RBA) configurations of OpenID Connect (OIDC) applications in Identity Authentication. Additionally, the service now supports the authorization server issuer identification in the authorization code flow, exposing this support in the authorization_response_iss_parameter_supported metadata field. [Data: Sources (1, 2), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 08), (2025, 04, 08))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between the Risk Management and Legal Compliance Departments, established in Q2 2000, ensures that risk mitigation strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at Enron. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (9), Date_Range ((2000, 04, 01), (2000, 07, 12))]\n\n## Continuous Integration & Delivery Updates\n\nThe Continuous Integration & Delivery team at SAP has resolved issues related to leading and trailing whitespaces in Cloud Foundry deployment configuration values and longer Git Clone URLs. These updates ensure smoother operations and improved user experience for developers. [Data: Sources (7, 8), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 08), (2025, 04, 08))]", "# SAP Technology Overview as of April 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's key technology departments, focusing on their recent updates and releases. The information is relevant to SAP's operations around April 2025.\n\n## Joule Multi-Language Support\n\nJoule now supports multiple languages, ensuring users experience Joule in their desired language. This feature automatically adopts the language configured within the SAP application and can understand languages other than those officially supported. This update is crucial for providing localized messages, product data, and more to users worldwide. [Data: Sources (67, 68), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 04), (2025, 04, 04))]\n\n## General Availability for Joule in SAP BTP Cockpit\n\nAfter a limited beta program, Joule in SAP BTP cockpit is now generally available with its first set of capabilities. It helps platform administrators ask questions related to their BTP resources, such as users or the runtime environment, in the cockpit. This update is essential for streamlining administrative tasks and improving operational efficiency. [Data: Source (68), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 01), (2025, 04, 04))]\n\n## New Date Field with Input Component\n\nA new Date field with input component has been introduced in SAP Build Apps, allowing users to provide date-picking functionality. This feature enables users to either manually type a date or select it from a calendar, enhancing user experience and productivity. [Data: 